{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer","id":1024863,"title":"Medium / Ghost Whisperer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-31T12:22:42-08:00","id":1024863,"title":"Medium / Ghost Whisperer","content":"One of my players is (very tentatively) brainstorming a new character, and one of the possible angles would involve ghosts in a positive-ish way. I.e. guiding them to the afterlife (whatever that may be), or separating them from their anger - more Medium / Ghost Whisperer than Necromancer.<br /> <br /> Looking at Arcana, we're not sure Death is a good fit despite dealing with ghosts - it seems to revolve around forcing ghosts and/or turning them into Mana candy, and that's cool but not what we want.<br /> <br /> So my question is: am I missing some subtlety of the Death arcanum that _does_ make it the right Sphere for us, or am I better off houseruling something (maybe a cross between Spirit, but affecting ghosts, and Death)? I'm the ST and more than happy to cobble something together here.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T12:31:05-08:00","id":1024865,"title":"","content":"Awakening magic isn't really a gentle thing. With it you can force ghosts to move on, but guiding them gently would require social interaction, or a lot of discrete manipulation of various other Arcana, which wouldn't really lead to guiding so much as manipulating. Using Mind to make people forget about the ghost, or accept that they've moved on, destroying Anchors or making them untenable, reshaping the ghost into something less angry, that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Death would, at the least, allow you to see and interact with ghosts, as well as find out about them. It would be the best foundation for further work, which would likely have to be done without magic, or at least would involve a lot of different magic, so as to 'solve' the ghost's dilemma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-31-2016, 03:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T12:40:03-08:00","id":1024869,"title":"","content":"That is what I was thinking, Have enough in Death Arcana to use Touch of the Grave and the Sigmund Freud them to talk them through their troubles and to help them move on, Some backup Arcana Might be mind and Fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:26:44-08:00","id":1024904,"title":"","content":"Being able to command them would be benifital in regards to allowing them to be helpful at times. An agressive ghost can be subdued through magic so you can speak with them. If you can't talk with them those commands can lubricate their willingness. With the death arcana you can also identify their anchor which is of great use. At I belive 4 dots you can also help it manifest, providing the manifestations not the conditions and so saving it essance. Another can strengthen a ghost and with mana raise a rank so a rank 1 ghost would gain sentience for 5he duration. <br /> <br /> It is easier to barter with spirits when you have spirit arcana than death with ghosts but it is still helpful. <br /> <br /> Another route I may suggest but may not be their way is trade favours for favours. In exchange for the mage helping the ghost pass on (it will take time) the ghost will help the mage. In a way this could even ease the ghosts worry. After all to offer everything but ask for nothing is suspicious. Binding a ghost to you (or having someone else bind it to you) as a familiar would also give the ghost the gift of freedom to move beyond their anchor so once again, you can give a boon while reciving one as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T14:55:12-08:00","id":1024912,"title":"","content":"Binding a ghost to you and making it your familiar is a Left Hand thing to do, That is what the Shadowbinders (from the Left Hand book) do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:09:34-08:00","id":1024915,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12802_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12802\" data-vbnamecard=\"12802\">Hardwire99</a> how is a default choice of familiar in 2e a lefthanded act? If it were shouldn't it be mentioned in the spell or merit? On the other hand if you were able to find a way bind it to your will, against its will then that'd be left handed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:11:45-08:00","id":1024916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hardwire99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1024912#post1024912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Binding a ghost to you and making it your familiar is a Left Hand thing to do, That is what the Shadowbinders (from the Left Hand book) do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghost familiars are somewhat common. The Shadowbinders were put forth as a debated upon legacy, as some don't think it's a big deal. Also, it involves absorbing the ghost's anchor into one's soul, which then changes the attitude of the mage and lowers their Wisdom. The act is different in many ways from simply offering the chance to be a familiar to a ghost, and they're considered a possible Left-handed legacy because they alter their own souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-31-2016, 06:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:30:20-08:00","id":1024921,"title":"","content":"The arcarna don't &quot;revolve&quot; around anything so narrow. Death is doing stuff with ghosts. You want to play nice, use it responsibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:40:04-08:00","id":1024924,"title":"","content":"It would be helpful to have 'detect Anchors' spell, that then let you destroy the Anchors connection to ghost and let him pass on by this, Question is, how much Death in dots do you need for this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T15:47:10-08:00","id":1024929,"title":"","content":"Death's Active Mage Sight lets you detect the Anchor Condition, but you could use the first dot's Speak with the Dead, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T16:19:10-08:00","id":1024937,"title":"","content":"Destroying an anchor is at least fraying, so 3 or 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T17:28:08-08:00","id":1024951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mistress of whispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer#post1024863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking at Arcana, we're not sure Death is a good fit despite dealing with ghosts - it seems to revolve around forcing ghosts and/or turning them into Mana candy, and that's cool but not what we want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Death can allow you to do the opposite of those things too. For instance you can bolster their existence, give them Essence, etc. So even if you want to play a nice necromancer Death is still -the- best arcana for dealing with ghosts. To be &quot;nice&quot; though you'd have to rely on your social skills, fortunately a command of Death gives you something to offer a ghost when you're trying to play nice. It's interesting that you assume guiding a ghost to the afterlife is a nice thing to do though, because the Underworld is where ghosts go and it's pretty hellish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1024924#post1024924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be helpful to have 'detect Anchors' spell, that then let you destroy the Anchors connection to ghost and let him pass on by this, Question is, how much Death in dots do you need for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Death Mage Sight or Speak with Dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T19:14:28-08:00","id":1024977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1024951#post1024951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's interesting that you assume guiding a ghost to the afterlife is a nice thing to do though, because the Underworld is where ghosts go and it's pretty hellish.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think the 'afterlife' in this situation would be whatever is beyond the Underworld, where ghosts <i>finally </i>go, as opposed to the Underworld, which is more of a lingering point between the real world and there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T21:36:49-08:00","id":1025002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1024977#post1024977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd think the 'afterlife' in this situation would be whatever is beyond the Underworld, where ghosts <i>finally </i>go, as opposed to the Underworld, which is more of a lingering point between the real world and there.</div> </div> </div> </div>For ghosts there isn't anything beyond that. Read the books. For souls there might be, but ghosts have an obvious final destination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T22:35:24-08:00","id":1025009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1025002#post1025002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For ghosts there isn't anything beyond that. Read the books. For souls there might be, but ghosts have an obvious final destination.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they resolve what their unresolved matters are I thought they moved on, not to the underworld but &quot;somewhere&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T22:41:07-08:00","id":1025010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1025009#post1025009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they resolve what their unresolved matters are I thought they moved on, not to the underworld but &quot;somewhere&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If that process does still exist, it's not common enough to warrant mentioning in any of the 2e ephemeral being mechanics so far, and the nearest direct equivalent in the edition at present is &quot;instances of the Anchor Condition based in unfinished business are resolved with that unfinished business's conclusion,&quot; which just removes one of the things keeping a ghost out of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Notably, the 1e Bound ceremony to let a ghost pass on had to be conducted in the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T00:46:18-08:00","id":1025025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1025002#post1025002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For ghosts there isn't anything beyond that. Read the books. For souls there might be, but ghosts have an obvious final destination.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's good advice. There's repeated mentions of 'beyond the Underworld' in the books, or at least another place or 'Final Reward' reached by the Pass On ritual of the Sin-Eaters that Satchel's mentioned. If you'll read, you'll note I said 'whatever is beyond the Underworld,' because it's a mystery that hasn't been clearly detailed. Merely theorized throughout Geist and other books and mentioned as a limitation in the abilities of the death gods, their powers not working on those who have passed 'beyond the Underworld.' They even have the theory, in-game, that there is an absolute nothing and whether you've passed peacefully or been annihilated as a ghost you reach the same place to the same effect, the only difference being your last moments.<br /> <br /> If you're of the mind that anything from first edition doesn't exist unless it's been explicitly called up in a second edition book, that's fair. Though the developer of Geist's second edition has stated <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/941893-geist-2nd-edition-thoughts-speculations?p=999603#post999603\">that the same mysterious fate of 'beyond' is what happens to those lucky few Integrity 10 who die, and never leave a ghost.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T10:22:20-08:00","id":1025103,"title":"","content":"I don't actually remember posting that, probably because it was New Year's Eve and I'd had a bit to drink. Anyway, sorry about the tone. I haven't read much of the Sin-Eater stuff and none of the Book of the Dead, most of my information about ghosts and the Underworld comes from the Mage books which I haven't seen make any mention of this &quot;place&quot; for ghosts beyond the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-01T12:17:03-08:00","id":1025131,"title":"","content":"It is pretty explicit that ghosts themselves are not actually souls, but rather lingering fragments of a soul that can't or won't pass on after death. That being said (and others have said), there's nothing stopping your character from treating ghosts like people and not being a dick with their Death magic. It might even be possible to somehow reunite a ghost who's resolved their anchors with the rest of their soul, which has passed beyond the Underworld. It's a Mystery!<br /> <br /> One of the theories put forth in the books (1E, granted) is that before the Fallen World and the rise of the Abyss souls would return to Stygia and from there cycle through the Supernal Realms before being reincarnated on Earth again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:14:35-08:00","id":1025334,"title":"","content":"Thanks so much for all the answers! We can definitely work with that.<br /> <br /> I have one more practical (if noobish, sorry) question: the book lists several one-dot Death powers (rotes?) after &quot;Initiate of Death&quot;. Can an Initiate cast any of these improvised, or does the player purchase each separately?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:20:08-08:00","id":1025336,"title":"","content":"All listed spells, and those created by Creative Thaumaturgy, can be cast as improvised spells and do not need to be a rote or praxis. The rotes and praxis just indicate which spells your particular character has invested study and therefore gains additional insight into their use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:20:45-08:00","id":1025337,"title":"","content":"If they have dots in the Arcana, they can cast any of them using improvised magic. They seem to be there to give you a grasp of the capabilities and give you a headstart on creating rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T01:54:11-08:00","id":1025340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1024863-medium-ghost-whisperer?p=1025337#post1025337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they have dots in the Arcana, they can cast any of them using improvised magic. They seem to be there to give you a grasp of the capabilities and give you a headstart on creating rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What he said.<br /> <br /> Look at the spells listed as an example of what magic can do and to show how magics fits into each purview. The real brawn behind spells is the Creative Thaumaturgy. That allows a mage to create and cast spells on the fly as improvised spell. The spells later is the basis for Rotes and Praxis. The theory and progression of spells is something like this.<br /> <br /> You imagine what you want your magic to do and through force of will and your enlightened wisdom cause it to happen. Your then cultivate that newly created spell, learning the intricacies of how it works learning how to further mold it until you are so familiar with it that it becomes a Praxis (easier to gain exceptional successes with) or it becomes a Rote (more powerful through the use of more reaches).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12802-hardwire99","name":"Hardwire99","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12802_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T02:32:37-08:00","id":1025348,"title":"","content":"Thanks again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Freelance Author and Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1713-mistress-of-whispers","name":"mistress of whispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1713_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T09:58:12-08:00","id":1025483,"title":"","content":"I made a spell to make ghosts free of their Anchors to let them pass on - for my take on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1025175-2e-fan-skalds\"><b>2E Skalds Legacy</b></a>. Here you go!<br /> <br /> <b>Resolve Anchor</b> (Death \u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Withstand:</b> Ghost\u2019s Rank<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Expression<br /> Merciful Disciples of Death can make ghosts free of their existence burden and just unravel their connection to material world, one by one, letting them pass to Afterlife. It works as taking out Anchors of ghost in question. Each connection is treated as one Target for the spell, so mage is taking multiple of them by rising Scale Factor. Note that sorcerer only destroys ghosts connection to Anchor, not the Anchor itself \u2013 so shades can be sure nothing bad will happen to their close ones or the things close to their life. Mage is aware of Anchors being over ghost, but to know where they are connected, he needs to use spells like <i>Know Ghost</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T17:15:37-08:00","id":1028336,"title":"","content":"You might find the following material from my game interesting.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/wikis/coven-of-the-summer-ash-legacy\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....mer-ash-legacy</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log/arachne-session-one\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....ne-session-one</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log/arachne-session-two\" target=\"_blank\">http://mage-doomcrew.obsidianportal....ne-session-two</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1470-johnny-awesome","name":"Johnny Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1470_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"447"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}